lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"flaky","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Deterministic reproduction recorded before the change (origin/main 57d45053272, 2026-11-17 PST). A scratch conftest wraps `rebar.reducer._cache.atomic_write` so that a rewrite of an existing path keeps that path's first mtime (`os.utime`), which models a coarse-timestamp filesystem. With it, `test_cache_invalidated_on_file_deletion` fails every time with `assert 1794938767.5136957 != 1794938767.5136957`. The same run's write log shows 2 cache writes, `(dir_hash 758d9db617d7, 1 comment)` then `(65d2f56cb3ad, 0 comments)`. So the reducer did recompute and rewrite the cache, and only the mtime oracle failed.","timestamp":1794939097945186084},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3414 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1), merged to main as d89abfa4e16b33733ea3e2bba566c8abb2811ad6. Evidence:\n- With the coarse_cache_mtime fixture active, both tests passed 20 of 20 runs.\n- Negative control: the old mtime oracle fails under the same fixture (`assert 1794939227.5500677 != 1794939227.5500677`).\n- `make verify` exited 0 on 8656fdd7884: 21343 passed, 30 skipped; integration tier 222 passed, 2 skipped.","timestamp":1794946524096911081}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794263069640294001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a7df9afc-b72f-44cf-bbc5-abfefeb2d114","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f86a-c0ce-f107-405f"},{"link_uuid":"2bc7ef06-aad2-4280-8dba-038cb5cc38af","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8d1d-d43c-0a3e-42d2"}],"description":"## Observation\n- `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_cache.py::test_cache_invalidated_on_file_deletion` (the assertion at line 180) checks that the `.cache.json` mtime changes between the warm write and the post-deletion rewrite. It compares float `st_mtime` values.\n- In an ubuntu:26.04 container on a colima VM (Linux 6.8.0-117-generic, aarch64, overlayfs /tmp), 2026-11-09 PST, the test failed 16 of 30 runs with no sandbox and 18 of 30 under bwrap. Every failure read `assert 1794262869.4604867 != 1794262869.4604867`.\n- It passes on GitHub's hosted runners. It is in the `reducer-processors` mutation shard, so a failure there fails that shard's clean baseline.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed 2026-11-17 PST, origin/main 57d45053272)\n- The cache is rewritten correctly. Only the test's oracle depends on timestamp granularity.\n- Deterministic reproduction: a scratch conftest wraps `rebar.reducer._cache.atomic_write` (the only cache write seam, `src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py:117`). After each rewrite of an existing path, it sets that path's mtime back to the first write's value with `os.utime`. This models a filesystem whose timestamp tick is coarser than the gap between the two writes.\n- Result: the test fails every time with the reported shape (`assert 1794938767.5136957 != 1794938767.5136957`). The write log shows the second `reduce_ticket` did rewrite the cache, with a new `dir_hash` (`758d9db617d7` then `65d2f56cb3ad`) and 0 comments.\n- So the \"no rewrite on those hosts\" hypothesis is refuted, and the failure is an mtime-granularity artifact of the oracle.\n- The same oracle class appears at line 372 of the same file, in `test_cache_miss_on_same_size_inplace_rewrite`, as `st_mtime_ns == before` to prove a cache HIT. On a coarse-timestamp host that check passes even when the cache was rewritten, so it cannot detect a regression there. Same cause, opposite symptom.\n\n## Approach\nProve whether the cache was rewritten from facts that do not depend on clock granularity.\n- `atomic_write` always publishes through `tempfile.mkstemp` in the same directory plus `os.replace` (`src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py:102` and `:118`). The temp file exists alongside the old target until the replace, so every rewrite gives `.cache.json` a new inode, and an untouched cache keeps its inode.\n- The cache envelope's `dir_hash` and `state` fields (`_cache.py:116`) show what was written.\n- Change the two oracles:\n  - Deletion test: assert the inode changed, the envelope's `dir_hash` changed, and the cached `state` holds 0 comments.\n  - In-place-rewrite test: the cache-hit check asserts the inode is unchanged.\n- Add a module-local fixture to `test_reducer_cache.py` that applies the coarse-timestamp model above to both tests. It wraps `rebar.reducer._cache.atomic_write` with `monkeypatch` so that a rewrite of an existing path keeps the earlier mtime. Every run then executes both tests under the conditions of the failing host. The old mtime oracle fails deterministically there, and the new oracles must pass. This keeps the class from coming back.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_cache.py`: replace the two mtime oracles (lines ~162-183 and ~370-374) with inode plus envelope oracles, and add the module-local coarse-mtime fixture to those two tests. No production code changes.\n\n## Testing\n- Failure path: with the coarse-mtime fixture applied and the old mtime assertion kept, `test_cache_invalidated_on_file_deletion` fails (the reproduction above). Recorded on this ticket before the change.\n- Happy path: with the new oracles, both tests pass under the fixture, 20 of 20 runs (`pytest --count` is not installed, so a shell loop).\n- The rest of `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_cache.py` still passes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The root cause is identified with a deterministic reproduction (the coarse-mtime injection above, recorded on this ticket), and the test asserts cache recomputation in a way that does not depend on timestamp granularity. Checked by both tests passing 20 of 20 runs with the coarse-mtime fixture active.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0 on the change.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_cache.py","reason":"replace mtime rewrite oracles with inode + envelope oracles; module-local coarse-mtime fixture"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","8d1d-d43c-0a3e-42d2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"240345c7-5414-4555-ad23-f895df3d180f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d45f-229f-effe-4cf8","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_cache_invalidated_on_file_deletion fails about half the time on a coarse-timestamp Linux host (equal mtime after rewrite)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["88b25bbe-4a79-4c41-bb8e-0eed2d61e696","65833655-8a8e-4c09-a4a6-88583c4511f2","a8b5fe19-7abd-4caa-a75a-0a5d2da8b66c","f673f4b3-21c6-4d64-8b44-67910109a93c","e45ac7d6-5efc-45d7-8893-c2e67bb5cae9","c90fe220-4ef1-4dee-b577-2656195d78c5","2bc7ef06-aad2-4280-8dba-038cb5cc38af","1bab0c95-d269-4a9e-bada-b82b3a23ff8d","48800fb4-4026-41ff-a6a8-0a6cd442bef3","78274e9d-0597-44b4-913b-43230e38aed0","240345c7-5414-4555-ad23-f895df3d180f","ed10cdcc-7619-4b3a-a94e-f1aae3bb1f39"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794946677474644058,"uuid":"dca8b1bd-02d5-429e-aed2-4f5bb9fd8450"}
